## UI Kit location and naming

- New Tailwind/NativeWind UI primitives MUST live in [`src/components/ui/`](mdc:src/components/ui/index.js).
- Name primitives with the `App` prefix to signal shared UI (e.g., `AppButton`, `AppInput`, `AppToggle`).
- Each primitive gets its own file (e.g., [`Button.js`](mdc:src/components/ui/Button.js)) and is re-exported via the barrel [`index.js`](mdc:src/components/ui/index.js).
- Props should be minimal and consistent across primitives:
  - `size`: 'sm' | 'md' (defaults to 'md').
  - `variant`: component-specific, but include 'primary' at minimum.
  - `className` and optional text-specific `textClassName` pass-throughs.
  - `disabled` where applicable.

## Tailwind usage

- Prefer Tailwind classes for structure and color; use inline numeric styles for calculated sizes only (heights, paddings derived from screen size).
- Avoid swapping many Tailwind classes at runtime; instead compute a small set of numeric values.
- Keep visual tokens (radii, spacing, colors) consistent with existing UI kit components.

## Responsive rules (useResponsive)

- Use [`useResponsive`](mdc:src/hooks/useResponsive.js) on screens that need size adaptations. Do NOT re-implement thresholds.
- Semantics from the hook:
  - `isVerySmallHeight` (≤568), `isSmallHeight` (≤667), plus `height` and `scale`.
  - Prefer a single small/very-small branch rather than many breakpoints.
- Pattern to follow (see [`LandingScreen.js`](mdc:src/containers/Onboard/Welcome/LandingScreen.js)):
  - Compute numeric paddings/heights from `height` with clamping.
  - Keep header typography stable per design (allow font scaling unless specified).
  - Use `ScrollView` only on very small heights to guarantee reachability.
  - Keep CTA button size consistent across devices unless explicitly required.

## Example usage (high level)

- Import primitives from the UI barrel:
  `import { AppButton } from 'src/components/ui';`
- In a screen: derive `topPadding`, `imageHeight`, etc., from `height` and clamp to sensible bounds. Apply via inline style while keeping Tailwind for layout/colors.

## Review checklist (PRs touching frontend)

- New primitives live under `src/components/ui/` and are exported from the barrel.
- Screens use `useResponsive` (not ad-hoc `Dimensions` logic) for size adaptations.
- Calculated sizes are numeric and clamped; minimal Tailwind class switching.
- No unnecessary `ScrollView` on large/medium sizes; enabled on very small heights only.

